cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: "If you use this analysis repository, cite the archived Zenodo code release when available and cite the associated research article once published."
title: "Purple sea urchin energetics under ocean warming, acidification, and thermal variability: R analysis code"
abstract: >-
  R code and supporting experimental data for analyzing physiological and
  energetic responses of Strongylocentrotus purpuratus to temperature,
  elevated seawater pCO2, and El Nino- and La Nina-like variable thermal regimes.
  Workflows cover resting metabolic rate, food consumption, assimilation
  efficiency, gonad production, food conversion efficiency, skeletal growth,
  Bayesian model fitting, and figure generation.
